It's a design pattern, the pattern defines a one to many dependency between objects and when one object (The Subject/Publisher)
changes state, all its dependents  (Observers/Subscribers) are notified and updated automatically.
so the subject has a list of observer objects, and it can remove or add them to the list.
It also notifies the registered ones when an event has occurred.

The observers/subscribers has only an update method and action, when they get updated they simply take action/don't take action
based on the required action.
